I built the C library with its CMake config, then wrote a [38;5;10mdlopen[0m-based differential harness ([38;5;10m/tmp/harness.c[0m) that drives both [38;5;10m.so[0ms through the same script and prints only address-independent values: hash vectors across seeds/lengths/alignments, array growth and capacity sequences, int-map put/get/get_ts/del over grow-shrink-rebuild cycles, string maps in all four [38;5;10mstring.mode[0m values, arena block splitting and oversized allocations, [38;5;10mstrkey[0m, and [38;5;10mhm_geti[0m at a dozen sizes. Output: [1m5487 lines, identical MD5[22m ([38;5;10mda8299a948cbe23f31bea914302d8f74[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Quirks deliberately preserved rather than fixed:[0m[0m
- In [38;5;10mstbds_siphash_bytes[0m, the byte-gathering expressions are [38;5;10mint[0m-typed, so [38;5;10md[3] << 24[0m overflows and sign-extends when widened to [38;5;10msize_t[0m, wiping the high 32 bits. Reproduced via [38;5;10m(x as i32).wrapping_shl(24) as isize as usize[0m. The harness targets this case explicitly.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstbds_hmput_key[0m updates [38;5;10mtemp_key[0m when a key is matched in the first bucket scan but [3mnot[23m in the wrap-around scan. Reproducing this is what makes a [38;5;10mshputs[0m-style caller corrupt keys and later trip an assertion — same in both builds.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstbds_arrfreef(NULL)[0m frees a wild pointer; [38;5;10mstbds_arrgrowf(NULL, n, 0, 0)[0m returns [38;5;10mNULL[0m.[0m[0m
- The [38;5;10mswitch (len - i)[0m fallthrough chain and the exact order of error/validation checks are preserved.[0m[0m
